  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The book consists of 17 quires each comprising 5 bifolia and 1 quire at end comprising 6 bifolia.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The pages of this artist's book display grid lines similar to a map with Cartesian coordinates. The grid lines gradually narrow toward the center of the book and then widen again. The book includes a book jacket and several sheets of paper printed with a stone pattern. The sheets of paper can be kneaded into a three dimensional object that can be placed on the grid lines and thus become a reference to a boulder, a rock, a hill, a lake, etc.</subfield>
  </datafield>
